the namespace on a specialization, and cl's own initializer_list. cxx1 spells V?$initializer_list@H@@ where cl spells V?$initializer_list@H@std@@ - templates are keyed here by their bare name, so a specialization does not know which namespace it came from, which docs/CONFORMANCE.md records - and cl builds against its own std::initializer_list where cxx1 builds against include/initializer_list, so its constructors are symbols cxx1 has none of and cxx1's begin/end/size are symbols cl has none of. initializer-list-construction.nocl records the same pair for the same header. What this case is about, that `Row r({1, 2})` and `Grid g({ {1,2}, {3,4} })` build through the initializer_list constructor, is checked by run-cases.cmd on the box and run.sh on the other two.
